      "writtenOn": "2026-10-09T06:19:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Nobuto,\n\nSunbeam won\u0027t allow two cinder backends to specify same volume_backend_name value. If second backend uses the same name, it will go into blocked state with the message. This is aligned with the ticket expectation \u0027If Sunbeam intends to require uniqueness, it should reject the configuration with a clear error rather than silently ignoring it.\u0027",
      "parentUuid": "774f3830_8be8690f",
      "revId": "ef08b33e0e58f9222904cf1c27872639876121b0",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5f3643a_1082d180",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8108
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-09T06:23:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the comment has the context around it.\n\n\u003e Expected: multiple backends sharing a volume_backend_name is standard Cinder configuration and is how pooling across backends is expressed (https://docs.openstack.org/cinder/latest/admin/multi-backend.html). It works as expected on Kolla-Ansible deployments. If Sunbeam intends to require uniqueness, it should reject the configuration with a clear error rather than silently ignoring it.\n\nThe first preference is of course supporting the architecture since it\u0027s pretty common design pattern of Cinder deployment, and the upstream supports it 100%.",
      "parentUuid": "e6eea76e_3d850a48",
      "revId": "ef08b33e0e58f9222904cf1c27872639876121b0",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
